{"id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone","title":"thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone","path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry.md","line":363,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry.tex#thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone","uses":["[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone]]","[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric]]","[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry.tex","label":"thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone","line":520,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Existence of the tangent cone]\n\\label{thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone}\n\\source{chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0429}\n\\uses{def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone, prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric, thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity}\n\\dcref{appG:G.49}\\group{Aleksandrov structure}\n\nIf $X$ is $n$-dimensional Aleksandrov with curvature $\\geq k$, then $T_pX$\nexists, has nonnegative curvature, and is isometric to the Euclidean cone over\nthe completed space of directions $\\Sigma_p$.  For $n\\geq3$, $\\Sigma_p$ is\ncompact of curvature at least $1$; if $\\Sigma_p\\cong S^{n-1}(1)$, then $p$ has\na neighborhood homeomorphic to an open subset of $\\R^n$.\n\\end{theorem}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Existence of the tangent cone] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a63686f772d6969692d6734392d74616e67656e742d636f6e65\"></span> <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0429</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fappg-elementary-metric-geometry%23def%3Achow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone\">↗ def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fappg-elementary-metric-geometry%23prop%3Achow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric\">↗ prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fappg-elementary-metric-geometry%23thm%3Achow-iii-g40-g42-regularity\">↗ thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. appG:G.49</span></span>\\group Aleksandrov structure <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X$\">$X$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-dimensional Aleksandrov with curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\geq k$\">$\\geq k$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pX$\">$T_pX$</span> exists, has nonnegative curvature, and is isometric to the Euclidean cone over the completed space of directions <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Sigma _p$\">$\\Sigma _p$</span>. For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n\\geq 3$\">$n\\geq 3$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Sigma _p$\">$\\Sigma _p$</span> is compact of curvature at least <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>; if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Sigma _p\\cong S^{n-1}(1)$\">$\\Sigma _p\\cong S^{n-1}(1)$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> has a neighborhood homeomorphic to an open subset of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\R ^n$\">$\\R ^n$</span>. ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group"]},"previous":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#rem:chow-iii-g47-volume-comparison","next":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#def:chow-iii-g50-exponential-cut-locus","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone","title":"def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone","label":"def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric","title":"prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric","label":"prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity","title":"thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity","label":"thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#def:chow-iii-g50-exponential-cut-locus","title":"def:chow-iii-g50-exponential-cut-locus","label":"def:chow-iii-g50-exponential-cut-locus"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#thm:chow-iii-g52-aleksandrov-stratification","title":"thm:chow-iii-g52-aleksandrov-stratification","label":"thm:chow-iii-g52-aleksandrov-stratification"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone","title":"thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[Existence of the tangent cone]\n\\label{thm:chow-iii-g49-tangent-cone}\n\\source{chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0429}\n\\uses{def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone, prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric, thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity}\n\\dcref{appG:G.49}\\group{Aleksandrov structure}\n\nIf $X$ is $n$-dimensional Aleksandrov with curvature $\\geq k$, then $T_pX$\nexists, has nonnegative curvature, and is isometric to the Euclidean cone over\nthe completed space of directions $\\Sigma_p$.  For $n\\geq3$, $\\Sigma_p$ is\ncompact of curvature at least $1$; if $\\Sigma_p\\cong S^{n-1}(1)$, then $p$ has\na neighborhood homeomorphic to an open subset of $\\R^n$.\n\\end{theorem}","source":"tex/references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone","title":"def:chow-iii-g29-euclidean-cone","description":""},{"node":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric","title":"prop:chow-iii-g30-g32-cone-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity","title":"thm:chow-iii-g40-g42-regularity","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}